      "text": "To find the new class mean after all 36 students have taken the test, we need to calculate the total score for all students and then divide by the number of students.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total score for the 30 students who took the test initially. The mean score for these 30 students is 72%. Therefore, the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[ 72 \\times 30 = 2160 \\text{ points} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total score for the 6 students who took the test later. The mean score for these 6 students is 78%. Therefore, the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[ 78 \\times 6 = 468 \\text{ points} \\]\n\nNow, we find the total score for all 36 students by adding the total scores of the two groups:\n\\[ 2160 + 468 = 2628 \\text{ points} \\]\n\nFinally, we find the new class mean by dividing the total score by the total number of students:\n\\[ \\frac{2628}{36} = 73 \\]\n\nThus, the new class mean is \\(\\boxed{73}\\).",
