      "text": "To find the new class mean, we need to calculate the total score of all the students and then divide by the total number of students.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total score of the 30 students who took the test initially. The mean score of these 30 students is 72%. Therefore, the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[\n30 \\times 72 = 2160\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the total score of the 6 students who took the test on the next day. The mean score of these 6 students is 78%. Therefore, the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[\n6 \\times 78 = 468\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the total scores of both groups to find the overall total score of the class:\n\\[\n2160 + 468 = 2628\n\\]\n\nThe total number of students in the class is:\n\\[\n30 + 6 = 36\n\\]\n\nTo find the new class mean, we divide the overall total score by the total number of students:\n\\[\n\\frac{2628}{36} = 73\n\\]\n\nThus, the new class mean is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{73}\n\\]",
